WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Type I covers small appliances. Don't underestimate this section — it has tricky
questions.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Type I covers factory-charged systems containing 5 lbs or less of refrigerant.
This includes window AC units, PTACs, household refrigerators, freezers,
dehumidifiers, water coolers, and vending machines. These systems are

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Small Appliance: Factory-charged system with 5 lbs or less of refrigerant.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
PTAC: Packaged Terminal Air Conditioner. Self-contained unit installed through a
wall.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Many entry-level jobs involve servicing
small appliances in hotels, restaurants, and residential settings.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: 5 lbs is the cutoff for small appliances. And —
Factory-charged means sealed at the factory

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
What is the maximum charge that defines a small appliance under EPA 608? That
number is on the exam.

